WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.070
1817.

2
00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:06.770
The economist David Ricardo imagines
two countries and two goods:

3
00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:08.450
cloth and wine.

4
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:12.970
In England, a year's cloth
takes the work of 100 workers.

5
00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:14.990
Wine takes 120.

6
00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:18.410
In Portugal, cloth takes 90 workers.

7
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.210
Wine takes just 80.

8
00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:22.750
Portugal needs fewer workers for both.

9
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.390
So why trade at all?

10
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:27.130
Shouldn't Portugal just
make everything itself?

11
00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:30.270
In this mission, you'll work
through Ricardo's table yourself,

12
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:34.750
and see why places that have what
others need trade with each other.

13
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:40.690
Then you'll see how the WTO, trade blocs
and tariffs shape where goods flow today.

14
00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:44.930
Your mission: find out why Portugal
and England would trade at all.
